wmba/mesh_utils.py contains code adapted from Vox2Cortex:

    normalize_vertices_per_max_dim      from vox2organ/utils/coordinate_transform.py
    unnormalize_vertices_per_max_dim    from vox2organ/utils/coordinate_transform.py
    aggregate_trilinear                 from vox2organ/utils/feature_aggregation.py
    aggregate_from_indices              from vox2organ/utils/feature_aggregation.py

Modifications made here: shared assertion logic factored into a helper;
`aggregate_from_indices` now honours its `mode` argument (upstream and the
earlier version of this code silently forced bilinear interpolation);
`aggregate_trilinear` raises on an empty selection rather than failing inside
torch.cat.

get_occupied_voxels_trimesh implements the same idea as Vox2Cortex's
Mesh.get_occupied_voxels, though not by copying it; voxelize_mesh_trimesh and
normalize_vertices_flip have no upstream counterpart.

